1
00:00:14,200 --> 00:00:18,000
!Don't

2
00:00:20,480 --> 00:00:21,310
get up!

3
00:00:29,120 --> 00:00:30,680
Shut it up!

4
00:01:03,920 --> 00:01:05,320
Oh

5
00:01:32,900 --> 00:01:33,730
Lush,

6
00:01:33,940 --> 00:01:37,197
green forests as far as the eye can see,

7
00:01:37,280 --> 00:01:41,020
gentle stream with crystal clear water,

8
00:01:41,420 --> 00:01:46,940
flowers and plants teeming with color and
life, beautiful beaches in every region.

9
00:01:47,260 --> 00:01:49,760
This is a tale of the land of Wano,

10
00:01:50,140 --> 00:01:52,457
when its skies were clear and its people

11
00:01:52,540 --> 00:01:56,077
flourished in a paradise
secluded from the world.

12
00:01:56,160 --> 00:02:00,560
You're saying that a mountain
was chasing you? That's right!

13
00:02:00,720 --> 00:02:03,220
And the thing was groaning at us, too!

14
00:02:04,160 --> 00:02:05,037
An ill omen!

15
00:02:05,120 --> 00:02:08,120
Perhaps you awakened the
wrath of the mountain god.

16
00:02:10,020 --> 00:02:10,980
Just kidding.

17
00:02:11,280 --> 00:02:14,692
But you look quite happy after
such a frightful encounter.

18
00:02:14,900 --> 00:02:16,018
What else happened?

19
00:02:16,540 --> 00:02:17,716
Can't fool you, huh?

20
00:02:17,800 --> 00:02:19,035
We finally caught it!

21
00:02:28,240 --> 00:02:30,180
What an adorable little boar!

22
00:02:30,720 --> 00:02:34,257
If we take it to the capital,
we'll get a platinum coin for him!

23
00:02:34,340 --> 00:02:35,170
What?!

24
00:02:35,300 --> 00:02:38,006
You could buy a house
with that kind of money!

25
00:02:38,420 --> 00:02:40,837
The boss of the Kurokoma
family has been looking

26
00:02:40,920 --> 00:02:43,437
for a white boar to put on
display in his storefront!

27
00:02:43,520 --> 00:02:46,638
He had a reward poster put
out for it and everything!

28
00:02:47,160 --> 00:02:49,219
But he shouldn't put it on display!

29
00:02:49,880 --> 00:02:53,000
White boars are divine
messengers, not decorations!

30
00:02:55,400 --> 00:02:56,230
Hmm?

31
00:02:58,740 --> 00:02:59,570
Kin'emon?

32
00:02:59,960 --> 00:03:00,790
Ow!

33
00:03:01,020 --> 00:03:01,937
Ow! Ow! Ow! Ow!

34
00:03:02,020 --> 00:03:02,850
Ow!

35
00:03:02,933 --> 00:03:05,060
Stealing money from our
shop again, are you? Zuru!

36
00:03:05,480 --> 00:03:07,357
We've known each other since childhood!

37
00:03:07,440 --> 00:03:08,397
Give me a break here!

38
00:03:08,480 --> 00:03:09,539
We're like family!

39
00:03:09,640 --> 00:03:11,237
You can spare a little money for me!

40
00:03:11,320 --> 00:03:13,237
You're just going to gamble it all away!

41
00:03:13,320 --> 00:03:14,777
Do you know how much you owe me?

42
00:03:14,860 --> 00:03:16,213
Because I certainly do!

43
00:03:19,760 --> 00:03:22,900
The next time you lay your
filthy fingers on mine,

44
00:03:24,220 --> 00:03:27,560
I'll sell your organs to cover the debt.

45
00:03:28,780 --> 00:03:32,680
If you can't pay me back, I'll
take your clothes as cool.

46
00:03:43,220 --> 00:03:45,500
Oh, please don't cry right here.

47
00:03:45,660 --> 00:03:49,200
Although a funeral is the proper
place for that, I suppose,

48
00:03:49,460 --> 00:03:50,497
since something happened.

49
00:03:50,580 --> 00:03:52,057
Not with the service, no.

50
00:03:52,140 --> 00:03:56,157
But after the cremation, when we were
about to gather up my father's bones,

51
00:03:56,240 --> 00:03:57,320
he showed up!

52
00:03:57,740 --> 00:04:02,093
He put a pot on top of the remains and
started cooking Odin with the fire!

53
00:04:08,180 --> 00:04:11,580
It seems the young Lord Odin
has no talent for sailing.

54
00:04:12,080 --> 00:04:17,460
As of today, he has attempted to
leave the country illegally 38 times.

55
00:04:17,760 --> 00:04:19,819
Rather impressive that he survived.

56
00:04:20,240 --> 00:04:22,217
I suspect that you know much of this,

57
00:04:22,300 --> 00:04:26,535
but allow me to offer a glimpse into
some of your son's accomplishments.

58
00:04:26,640 --> 00:04:30,700
Before he was even a year
old, he sent his nanny flying.

59
00:04:30,960 --> 00:04:34,457
When he was two, he was swift
enough to catch two hares at once.

60
00:04:34,540 --> 00:04:38,128
When he was four, he hurled a
boulder and knocked out a bear.

61
00:04:38,540 --> 00:04:43,197
When he was six, he spent all his time at
the pleasure halls wasting royal money.

62
00:04:43,280 --> 00:04:44,339
When he was eight,

63
00:04:44,480 --> 00:04:46,477
for some reason he
instigated a fight with a

64
00:04:46,560 --> 00:04:48,777
bunch of violent patrons
at a gambling parlor.

65
00:04:48,860 --> 00:04:50,742
He defeated them all, naturally.

66
00:04:50,860 --> 00:04:54,300
By the time he was nine, he
was blacklisted by the Yakuza.

67
00:04:54,920 --> 00:04:58,657
He repaid this slight by burning down
the gambling hall he was banned from,

68
00:04:58,740 --> 00:05:00,120
instigating a gang war.

69
00:05:00,320 --> 00:05:04,720
Then, at the ripe age of ten years
old, he was arrested for assault.

70
00:05:05,160 --> 00:05:07,017
Sent to the quarries as punishment,

71
00:05:07,100 --> 00:05:10,457
he developed an impressive talent
while serving his sentence.

72
00:05:10,540 --> 00:05:14,120
That is to say, he became a
master stonemason in no time,

73
00:05:14,320 --> 00:05:16,800
thanks, of course, to his Kozuki blood.

74
00:05:18,340 --> 00:05:21,460
From there, he left prison
and reformed his ways

75
00:05:22,040 --> 00:05:26,457
Then there's the tale of the drought
When wells were drying up in the capital,

76
00:05:26,540 --> 00:05:29,364
he couldn't bear the sight
of people's suffering

77
00:05:30,080 --> 00:05:33,962
So when he was 14, he redirected
the river to run through the city

78
00:05:36,120 --> 00:05:40,660
This caused a massive flood And
an arrest warrant was issued again

79
00:05:42,120 --> 00:05:45,157
This was his cue to flee
So he traversed that

80
00:05:45,240 --> 00:05:48,840
river in hopes of escaping
the country by sea.

81
00:05:50,560 --> 00:05:52,900
Needless to say, he failed miserably.

82
00:05:53,680 --> 00:05:58,457
Then, when he was 15, he threatened a
priest to let him hide in a mountain temple.

83
00:05:58,540 --> 00:06:01,640
He brought back women from
the capital every night.

84
00:06:01,940 --> 00:06:04,160
Before long, he had his own harem.

85
00:06:06,660 --> 00:06:09,617
This is clearly the work
of a monster and not a man.

86
00:06:09,700 --> 00:06:10,640
That said,

87
00:06:10,940 --> 00:06:15,357
although he did acquire a great many
lovers, they were free to leave at any time.

88
00:06:15,440 --> 00:06:18,960
Of course, not everyone
involved was quite so happy.

89
00:06:19,220 --> 00:06:23,632
The women's boyfriends, for example,
and their parents, and their husbands.

90
00:06:23,840 --> 00:06:26,980
A team of skillful samurai
even joined their cause.

91
00:06:29,180 --> 00:06:32,840
The young lord welcomed their
challenge and stood his ground.

92
00:06:34,740 --> 00:06:37,477
This later came to be
known as the harem war.

93
00:06:37,560 --> 00:06:40,640
The Hilgaro family
attempted to restore peace.

94
00:06:40,800 --> 00:06:45,037
But when all attempts failed, they were
drawn into the chaos of battle as well.

95
00:06:45,120 --> 00:06:46,200
I've heard enough.

96
00:06:47,760 --> 00:06:48,590
Right.

97
00:06:48,740 --> 00:06:51,220
The young lord is now 18 years old.

98
00:06:51,500 --> 00:06:55,147
He continues to stir up trouble
at a healthy pace to this day.

99
00:06:55,400 --> 00:06:56,230
Report over.

100
00:06:56,400 --> 00:07:00,282
I need you to deliver this to Odin
without speaking on the matter.

101
00:07:04,940 --> 00:07:06,777
It's like I just won the lottery.

102
00:07:06,860 --> 00:07:09,620
My lucky star is shining on me today.

103
00:07:10,600 --> 00:07:14,880
If I give this to old boss
Kurokoma, I'll be rich!

104
00:07:16,900 --> 00:07:20,606
Hey, while we're at it, how about
you give me all your clothes?

105
00:07:25,600 --> 00:07:27,517
You're not getting away this time!

106
00:07:27,600 --> 00:07:28,657
Whoa, whoa, whoa, wait!

107
00:07:28,740 --> 00:07:29,681
Give me a break!

108
00:07:30,100 --> 00:07:31,677
I'll pay you guys back today!

109
00:07:31,760 --> 00:07:33,017
I'm about to hit it big!

110
00:07:33,100 --> 00:07:35,097
More excuses! It's true!

111
00:07:35,180 --> 00:07:37,474
Just let me go to the Kurokoma Mansion!

112
00:07:39,820 --> 00:07:40,650
Kin'emon?

113
00:07:40,733 --> 00:07:41,563
Oh, him?

114
00:07:41,646 --> 00:07:43,780
That little thug who stole our money?

115
00:07:44,420 --> 00:07:46,580
Well, here's an easy solution.

116
00:07:46,820 --> 00:07:48,617
Catch him and fillet him alive.

117
00:07:48,700 --> 00:07:50,880
But don't engage him one-on-one.

118
00:07:51,320 --> 00:07:53,380
He's a punk, but he's strong.

119
00:07:53,800 --> 00:07:54,860
Real strong.

120
00:07:57,320 --> 00:07:59,740
I have been entrusted with 60 silver.

121
00:07:59,960 --> 00:08:02,097
But simply spending it would be a waste.

122
00:08:02,180 --> 00:08:03,010
Right?

123
00:08:05,180 --> 00:08:06,760
I'll take this pot here.

124
00:08:07,440 --> 00:08:09,357
I'm running an errand for someone.

125
00:08:09,440 --> 00:08:10,270
All right.

126
00:08:10,353 --> 00:08:11,375
That'll be 30 silver.

127
00:08:11,900 --> 00:08:13,320
Here. Thanks, kid.

128
00:08:14,780 --> 00:08:16,720
Oops, I bought the wrong pot.

129
00:08:17,240 --> 00:08:19,020
I needed the bigger one.

130
00:08:20,120 --> 00:08:23,460
All right, but that
one is 60 silver. Easy.

131
00:08:23,720 --> 00:08:27,955
I paid you 30 for the first pot, so
I'll give it back and that makes 60.

132
00:08:28,320 --> 00:08:29,150
Got it.

133
00:08:29,740 --> 00:08:30,600
Thanks, pal.

134
00:08:32,520 --> 00:08:33,557
What the hell?

135
00:08:33,640 --> 00:08:36,405
Well, he just conned that
guy out of 30 silver.

136
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:39,060
Easy money.

137
00:08:39,940 --> 00:08:41,120
Psst, dingito.

138
00:08:41,280 --> 00:08:42,800
Oh, Cain, you scared me.

139
00:08:44,260 --> 00:08:47,040
Look, I scored me something good.

140
00:09:17,140 --> 00:09:18,940
Oh, Suso.

141
00:09:22,600 --> 00:09:26,340
Our next drink will be in the afterlife.

142
00:09:32,740 --> 00:09:34,280
Take it easy, friend

143
00:09:39,840 --> 00:09:44,980
Excuse me I'll be taking my
leave But I'm sorry for your loss

144
00:09:56,360 --> 00:09:58,680
That was amazing. So cool.

145
00:09:59,300 --> 00:10:00,660
What did he just do?

146
00:10:01,060 --> 00:10:03,740
That was one of his
trademark Odin speeches.

147
00:10:06,440 --> 00:10:09,080
Just to be clear, you came to arrest me.

148
00:10:09,800 --> 00:10:10,760
Well, yes.

149
00:10:11,080 --> 00:10:14,897
But personally, I don't want to
arrest you, so if you could bribe me,

150
00:10:14,980 --> 00:10:16,392
that would help us both.

151
00:10:18,640 --> 00:10:19,860
Well, this is new.

152
00:10:20,800 --> 00:10:23,117
Usually it's me people are running from.

153
00:10:23,200 --> 00:10:25,297
Ah, there must be a fire
or something of the sort.

154
00:10:25,380 --> 00:10:27,340
Are you out of your mind?

155
00:10:27,680 --> 00:10:30,092
You can't bring that thing into the city!

156
00:10:31,040 --> 00:10:31,870
What?

157
00:10:31,953 --> 00:10:33,000
But it's just a little boar!

158
00:10:33,540 --> 00:10:35,557
Kurokoma doesn't want that for business!

159
00:10:35,640 --> 00:10:39,169
He wants to use it as a decoy
to destroy the Hyogoro family!

160
00:10:39,280 --> 00:10:40,456
What does that mean?

161
00:10:40,640 --> 00:10:43,077
I mean that thing's
parent will come for it!

162
00:10:43,160 --> 00:10:46,866
We'll have a giant boar charging
through town in his nevel now!

163
00:10:52,560 --> 00:10:53,480
Up I go!

164
00:10:59,900 --> 00:11:01,665
What do you mean, it's parrot?

165
00:11:01,920 --> 00:11:05,657
According to ancient documents, it's
white and strong and big as a mountain.

166
00:11:05,740 --> 00:11:08,577
Why do you think everyone
calls it the mountain god?

167
00:11:08,660 --> 00:11:09,490
What?

168
00:11:09,660 --> 00:11:12,220
They say that several hundred years ago,

169
00:11:12,340 --> 00:11:14,877
it destroyed an entire
village in one night.

170
00:11:14,960 --> 00:11:18,200
That sounded crazy, so I
figured it was just a legend.

171
00:11:18,920 --> 00:11:23,517
But now, there's a white boar
here right in front of our eyes.

172
00:11:23,600 --> 00:11:29,057
so that must mean the
mountain god is real it's come

173
00:11:29,140 --> 00:11:33,700
to swallow us alive it's
already upon us run for it

174
00:11:42,100 --> 00:11:46,540
it's all our fault the capital's
doomed and it's my fault

175
00:11:53,960 --> 00:11:55,360
Oh,

176
00:11:55,720 --> 00:12:01,140
my God.

177
00:12:17,220 --> 00:12:18,260
Kozuki Oden!

178
00:12:20,360 --> 00:12:23,831
Pardon me, I couldn't help but
overhear what you just said.

179
00:12:24,600 --> 00:12:27,482
I don't need to know how
you came upon that boar.

180
00:12:28,620 --> 00:12:30,860
But why don't you hand it over to me?

181
00:12:31,300 --> 00:12:33,020
And I'll settle this.

182
00:12:49,460 --> 00:12:51,697
Well, thanks a lot, you little pork chop.

183
00:12:51,780 --> 00:12:53,280
Now we're all gonna die.

184
00:12:54,120 --> 00:12:55,002
Stop squealing.

185
00:12:55,360 --> 00:12:57,654
I told you, just give that thing to me.

186
00:12:57,840 --> 00:12:59,020
Now, hold on a sec.

187
00:12:59,200 --> 00:13:00,237
You can't take this from me.

188
00:13:00,320 --> 00:13:01,557
I'm gonna sell it and get rich.

189
00:13:01,640 --> 00:13:04,957
So hands off, I've got a mountain of
debts I need to pay off right away.

190
00:13:05,040 --> 00:13:08,197
Then I'm gonna use the rest on
investments to get even more rich.

191
00:13:08,280 --> 00:13:09,360
That's really him?

192
00:13:10,260 --> 00:13:11,090
Kotakiyotin?

193
00:13:11,640 --> 00:13:13,477
Adults are nothing but a bunch of clowns.

194
00:13:13,560 --> 00:13:17,280
But this man, this man alone, I respect.

195
00:13:24,160 --> 00:13:25,620
Its child is here.

196
00:13:25,880 --> 00:13:27,897
That's the only reason
why the mountain god

197
00:13:27,980 --> 00:13:29,757
would come to a place where humans dwell.

198
00:13:29,840 --> 00:13:32,957
You mean, some idiot stole
its child and brought it here?

199
00:13:33,040 --> 00:13:35,657
We must placate the
mountain god and quickly.

200
00:13:35,740 --> 00:13:38,377
There should be a white
piglet somewhere close by.

201
00:13:38,460 --> 00:13:43,401
If we can't send it back to the mountain
where it belongs, the capital will drop us.

202
00:13:49,400 --> 00:13:51,440
Help, I'm stuck! Somebody!

203
00:13:53,580 --> 00:13:56,560
This moving house is people and all!

204
00:13:56,660 --> 00:13:57,660
Daddy, no!

205
00:13:58,140 --> 00:13:59,140
It's a nightmare!

206
00:14:09,540 --> 00:14:11,937
So there you are, finally found you!

207
00:14:12,020 --> 00:14:14,257
This is all your fault, you boar thief!

208
00:14:14,340 --> 00:14:16,516
Who's the boar thief, you boar thief?

209
00:14:16,700 --> 00:14:19,497
Send that thing back to the
mountain before we're dead!

210
00:14:19,580 --> 00:14:22,077
You know what'll happen when
the big one gets a whiff of it?

211
00:14:22,160 --> 00:14:23,240
We're done for!

212
00:14:23,400 --> 00:14:24,820
It'll eat us! What?

213
00:14:25,100 --> 00:14:28,537
We had no idea this was gonna
happen when we took that piglet!

214
00:14:28,620 --> 00:14:31,914
My two buddies got eaten up
by the mountain god already!

215
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:34,529
The clothes smelled
like his baby, you see?

216
00:14:34,620 --> 00:14:37,326
And then it swallowed
your friend Tsuru, too!

217
00:14:37,540 --> 00:14:38,893
Wait, Tsuru was there?

218
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:41,497
We needed a plan to get that
white boar back from you!

219
00:14:41,580 --> 00:14:45,345
So we took Tsuru as a hostage,
but then on the way to the city,

220
00:14:47,280 --> 00:14:49,398
it came out of nowhere and ate them.

221
00:14:49,600 --> 00:14:51,776
They're dead and it's all your fault!

222
00:14:58,380 --> 00:14:59,240
Hey, wait!

223
00:15:08,200 --> 00:15:10,857
You know what'll happen when
the big one gets a whiff of it?

224
00:15:10,940 --> 00:15:13,080
We're done, boy! It's Alina!

225
00:15:17,140 --> 00:15:18,460
Out of my way!

226
00:15:21,380 --> 00:15:22,800
Here it comes!

227
00:15:36,340 --> 00:15:37,170
What?

228
00:15:37,420 --> 00:15:39,060
King stole something again?

229
00:15:39,320 --> 00:15:40,477
I'm so sorry.

230
00:15:40,560 --> 00:15:42,220
Please let me pay for it.

231
00:15:45,660 --> 00:15:47,800
Keen, it's time you get a real job.

232
00:15:48,160 --> 00:15:50,377
You can't keep angering
the Yakuza like this.

233
00:15:50,460 --> 00:15:52,000
They're going to kill you.

234
00:15:52,300 --> 00:15:53,240
So what?

235
00:15:53,520 --> 00:15:55,932
Not like anyone's going to care if I die.

236
00:16:00,220 --> 00:16:02,740
Did you just hit me with a rock?

237
00:16:03,840 --> 00:16:06,220
Give her back right there!

238
00:16:26,720 --> 00:16:29,000
Oh, my God.

239
00:16:45,780 --> 00:16:47,040
Stop it, you fool!

240
00:16:47,260 --> 00:16:50,537
If you haunt the mountain god, then
the land of water will pay the price!

241
00:16:50,620 --> 00:16:55,700
I'll cut you open, tear through your
belly, and I'll take Tsuru back!

242
00:16:56,180 --> 00:16:59,120
I don't care if you're a guy!

243
00:17:05,680 --> 00:17:06,510
Oh, no!

244
00:17:18,000 --> 00:17:18,960
Come on, team!

245
00:17:19,100 --> 00:17:20,100
Get out of there!

246
00:17:21,180 --> 00:17:23,680
I must admit, that fellow has guts.

247
00:17:40,560 --> 00:17:43,440
If Zuru dies because of me...

248
00:17:48,800 --> 00:17:51,160
...then I want to die, too.

249
00:18:16,580 --> 00:18:18,080
Hey! Four!

250
00:18:18,900 --> 00:18:21,140
This is what you're looking for!

251
00:18:22,980 --> 00:18:24,260
So it was you!

252
00:18:24,440 --> 00:18:25,616
I should have known!

253
00:18:26,060 --> 00:18:29,320
Kozuki Oden, the prodigal
son, at it again!

254
00:18:30,260 --> 00:18:32,240
You'll make a fine hot pot!

255
00:18:34,220 --> 00:18:35,600
This is the last straw!

256
00:18:35,720 --> 00:18:36,857
How could you do this?

257
00:18:36,940 --> 00:18:38,175
My mother was easily!

258
00:18:38,720 --> 00:18:39,550
Take that!

259
00:18:40,320 --> 00:18:41,880
No, you don't understand.

260
00:18:42,100 --> 00:18:43,600
My daughter is dead!

261
00:18:44,080 --> 00:18:46,120
I brought that boy here.

262
00:18:46,480 --> 00:18:49,200
It's my fault that the capital is ruined.

263
00:18:49,700 --> 00:18:52,160
Your loved ones are dead because of me.

264
00:19:05,300 --> 00:19:07,160
Oden, two-sword style!

265
00:19:51,520 --> 00:19:52,860
He's really something.

266
00:19:53,300 --> 00:19:54,600
Let's pack it up.

267
00:20:01,540 --> 00:20:05,477
They say that the people and houses
swallowed that day were so great

268
00:20:05,560 --> 00:20:09,677
in number that they could have formed
a new town in the boar's stomach.

269
00:20:09,760 --> 00:20:12,400
A quarter of the capital was destroyed,

270
00:20:12,780 --> 00:20:16,520
but miraculously, not a single
one of its citizens died.

271
00:20:16,880 --> 00:20:18,540
That was horrible!

272
00:20:25,880 --> 00:20:27,400
Odin was amazing.

273
00:20:28,340 --> 00:20:30,540
I almost cheered for him back there.

274
00:20:31,460 --> 00:20:34,420
I wish I could say thank you, but I can't.

275
00:20:34,600 --> 00:20:37,737
You saved us, but you're the
one who started this mess.

276
00:20:37,820 --> 00:20:39,260
Everyone, please listen.

277
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:42,200
It wasn't Odin's fault, it was...

278
00:20:43,780 --> 00:20:45,920
Don't do anything unnecessary.

279
00:20:46,400 --> 00:20:47,560
Poor Odin, sir!

280
00:20:49,440 --> 00:20:52,740
I'm sorry to give this to you
at a time of such revelry.

281
00:20:53,680 --> 00:20:54,820
Disavowed, am I?

282
00:20:55,080 --> 00:20:57,139
And expelled from the capital, too?

283
00:20:58,060 --> 00:20:59,300
Laughable shogun.

284
00:20:59,640 --> 00:21:00,580
Truly pathetic.

285
00:21:01,100 --> 00:21:03,840
So much power, and I'm
still too much for you.

286
00:21:04,040 --> 00:21:06,393
The capital cannot contain my greatness.

287
00:21:08,700 --> 00:21:14,840
Finally, I'll leave at once Wherever the
sun falls is where I shall sleep But now,

288
00:21:15,120 --> 00:21:18,957
I'm hungry The mountain
god incident marked a new

289
00:21:19,040 --> 00:21:22,334
beginning for Odin Who was
still quite young at the time

290
00:21:24,160 --> 00:21:25,240
What's the matter?

291
00:21:25,460 --> 00:21:32,260
Don't cry I'm not crying at all Listen,
I would die for that man, Tsuru Um,

292
00:21:32,600 --> 00:21:39,200
okay Well said, I would die for Lord
Odin too Hey! Digital! Wait! What? What?

293
00:21:39,680 --> 00:21:41,400
Kozuki Odin! Kozuki Odin!

294
00:21:41,520 --> 00:21:42,360
Kozuki Odin!

295
00:21:42,500 --> 00:21:44,880
That man is one of a kind! Indeed!

296
00:21:45,340 --> 00:21:47,928
And I'll follow him for
the rest of my life!

297
00:21:48,660 --> 00:21:50,200
I was his fan first!

298
00:21:50,400 --> 00:21:52,282
Yeah, well, I'm his biggest fan!

299
00:21:52,380 --> 00:21:53,733
And his first follower!

300
00:21:54,620 --> 00:21:56,860
I wish I was free like them!

301
00:21:57,380 --> 00:22:01,817
All the men who watched these events
transpire took a hesitant step forward,

302
00:22:01,900 --> 00:22:03,517
wishing that they could
go along with Odin.

303
00:22:03,600 --> 00:22:07,440
And thus the capital
tilted, ever so slightly.

304
00:22:10,920 --> 00:22:13,080
What an honor to see you, Lord Odin.

305
00:22:13,220 --> 00:22:14,455
Please come right in.

306
00:22:14,740 --> 00:22:17,681
Lord Yasui's been looking
forward to your arrival.

307
00:22:18,020 --> 00:22:19,920
Don't lie, I know he hasn't.

308
00:22:20,940 --> 00:22:22,580
That's right, you idiot.

309
00:22:22,900 --> 00:22:25,429
Who would look forward
to a visit from you?

310
00:22:25,700 --> 00:22:27,640
What is this, your entourage?

311
00:22:27,920 --> 00:22:29,397
What do you miscreants want?

312
00:22:29,480 --> 00:22:30,560
Hey, uncle!

313
00:22:30,900 --> 00:22:32,782
Oh, don't speak to me like that.

314
00:22:33,600 --> 00:22:34,440
Oh, wait!

315
00:22:34,640 --> 00:22:36,052
There's a puddle of mud!

316
00:22:38,140 --> 00:22:39,140
Please proceed.

317
00:22:39,520 --> 00:22:41,285
Better to walk across my back.

318
00:22:41,480 --> 00:22:42,715
Don't sully yourself.

319
00:22:44,240 --> 00:22:45,277
Who is this guy?

320
00:22:45,360 --> 00:22:46,360
He creeps me out!

321
00:22:46,480 --> 00:22:50,480
He's my new manservant, and you'd
best leave him alone. Ah, yes.

322
00:22:50,680 --> 00:22:53,020
Lord Yasui was very kind to take me in.

323
00:22:54,120 --> 00:22:55,355
Pleasure to meet you.

324
00:22:55,480 --> 00:22:56,960
I'm Kurozumi Oruji.
